# UI Components Development Guidelines

## Component Architecture
This project uses **Radix UI** primitives with **Tailwind CSS** and **class-variance-authority** for component variants.

## Base UI Components Location
All reusable UI components are in [apps/src/components/ui/](mdc:apps/src/components/ui/)

## Component Pattern Example
Reference the [Button component](mdc:apps/src/components/ui/button.tsx) for the standard pattern:

```tsx
import { cva, type VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority"
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"

const componentVariants = cva(
  "base-classes",
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        default: "default-styles",
        // ... other variants
      },
      size: {
        default: "default-size",
        // ... other sizes
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: "default",
      size: "default",
    },
  }
)

function Component({ className, variant, size, ...props }: 
  React.ComponentProps<"element"> & 
  VariantProps<typeof componentVariants>
) {
  return (
    <element 
      className={cn(componentVariants({ variant, size, className }))}
      {...props} 
    />
  )
}
```

## Required Imports
```tsx
import * as React from "react"
import { cva, type VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority"
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"
// Radix UI primitives as needed
import { Slot } from "@radix-ui/react-slot"
```

## Component Guidelines
- Use `cn()` utility from [apps/src/lib/utils.ts](mdc:apps/src/lib/utils.ts) for className merging
- Implement proper TypeScript interfaces extending `React.ComponentProps`
- Use `cva` for variant-based styling
- Support `asChild` pattern with Radix Slot when appropriate
- Include `data-slot` attributes for component identification
- Export both component and variants for external use